    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DRP101 · S1.5 · school slides</span>\n<h2>Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">10 slides, exactly as the university distributes them on FLM. A full lecture for this deck will be added later — for now, study the slides together with the session plan in Section 0 (lesson 0.5).</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DRP101 · S1.5 · slide của trường</span>\n<h2>Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">10 slide, đúng như trường phát trên FLM. Bài giảng chi tiết cho deck này sẽ bổ sung sau — trước mắt học theo slide cùng kế hoạch buổi ở Mục 0 (bài 0.5).</p></div>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · tài liệu sinh viên · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait.pptx</p>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/001.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 1: UNIT 5:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 1/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5:<br>DRAWING A FEMALE MODEL PORTRAIT</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/002.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 2: OBJECTIVES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 2/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>OBJECTIVES<br>(1 of 2)<br>- Distinguish female portrait characteristics.<br>- Revise knowledge about drawing a female model statue portrait.<br>- Reconstructing the entire knowledge of structure, portrait ratio, preparing knowledge for the analysis of the musculoskeletal structure of the next subject.<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/003.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 3: OBJECTIVES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 3/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>OBJECTIVES<br>(2 of 2)<br>- Analyze the similarities and differences between female and male portraits.<br>- Completing the skills of drawing and shading in the Drawing portrait lesson, preparing knowledge for the Drawing semibody and fullbody human model.<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/004.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 4: FACE SHAPES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 4/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>FACE SHAPES<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>There are characteristic differences between male and female portraits.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/005.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 5: DIFFERENCE FEATURES BETWEEN MALE AND FEMALE PORTRAITS\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 5/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>DIFFERENCE FEATURES BETWEEN MALE AND FEMALE PORTRAITS<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>(1 of 2)<br>Similar to the knowledge learned in the female model statue portrait, female portrait characteristics are often softer and more feminine than the masculinity of male models, the face of female models are more rounded compared to the angular of male models, the female model will have thicker and longer hair than the male model.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/006.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 6: DIFFERENCE FEATURES BETWEEN MALE AND FEMALE PORTRAITS\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 6/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>DIFFERENCE FEATURES BETWEEN MALE AND FEMALE PORTRAITS<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>(2 of 2)<br>- Female eyelashes are longer and curvier than male’s.<br>- The eyebrows of female are smaller and longer than those of male.<br>- Female eyes are usually bigger than male.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/007.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 7: SUMMARY\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 7/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>SUMMARY<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>There are differences in characteristics between male and female portrait. The way of rendering and shading is also a little different from the male model drawing, showing the feminine characteristics in the Drawing portrait lesson.<br>Eyelashes, eyebrows, eyes are different between male and female.<br>The block structure of female portraits is softer than male’s.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/008.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 8: PRACTICE EXERCISES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 8/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>PRACTICE EXERCISES<br>(1 of 2)<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>Practice exercises are carried out on A2 paper.<br>Completing the Drawing portrait skills through the process of structural analysis, light analysis.<br>Completing skills of rendering, segmenting, creating bold and pale strokes according to solid structure, brightness and character characteristics.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/009.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 9: PRACTICE EXERCISES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 9/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>PRACTICE EXERCISES<br>(2 of 2)<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait<br>Analyze and apply knowledge about the differences between portrait of male and female models in the Drawing. Understand the structure and characteristics of the female model's portrait to sketch, render, hatch and complete in order to make the drawing more vividly, describing the feminine feature. Creating emotions for the Drawing through the process of analyzing light, space and character characteristics.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DRP101/flm1/d05/010.webp\" alt=\"DRP101 · Unit 5 Drawing female model portrait · slide 10: PROJECT\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 10/10</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>PROJECT<br>Unit 5: Drawing a female model portrait</p></div>"
